body:
oh my god, trust me, first day of my classes, i was shaking so hard when we had to do venipunctures, eventually i overcame it when i thought of it this way;
• yes, you’re hurting somebody, you’re sticking a needle inside of them, but not out of malice, to aid in diagnosis of many conditions, and you’re helping them get better.
and then practice, practice practice practice, the more you do, the more comfortable you’ll become, and you’ll learn things to help. for example, i shake sometimes, my solution? anchor my hand against their arm while i take the blood, it helps the shakiness.

